# REQUEST-APP — Isolated Staging Configuration Example
#
# DO NOT copy secrets to git.
# DO NOT modify or overwrite your existing .env.local file.
#
# To connect your localhost development server to the staging backend without altering .env.local:
#
# Method 1 (Recommended — Zero file edits):
# Open your browser to:
# http://localhost:5173/?stagingUrl=https://script.google.com/macros/s/<STAGING_DEPLOYMENT_ID>/exec
# (The app verifies server-side staging identity before activating and confirms disposable spreadsheet association.)
#
# Method 2 (CLI Integration Test Runner without argument exposure):
# Set these in your terminal session before running:
# STAGING_PIN="<YOUR_STAGING_PIN>"
# node scripts/test-staging-backend.mjs "https://script.google.com/macros/s/<STAGING_DEPLOYMENT_ID>/exec" --confirm-staging
#
# Optional persistent spreadsheet ID verification:
# EXPECTED_STAGING_SHEET_ID="<DISPOSABLE_GOOGLE_SPREADSHEET_ID>"
